02835cam  2200433   u316182SIRSI20150811112635.0130918s2013    enka     b    001 0 eng d  aCGPbengerdacCGPdOCLCOdNYPdYDXCPdMLYdUPMdBTCTAdBDXdUKMGBdYBMdCDXdOCPdOCLCOdIH9dWAUdOCLCAdERASAdZLMdOCLCOdNJMdOCLCFdCHVBKdYJLdIADdNYWWBdOCLCQ  c$1  aGBB3762812bnb  a9780714865751  a0714865753  a(OCoLC)858843038 4aN7340b.C486 2013  aTNTA04aThe Chinese art book /ccontributors, Colin Mackenzie, Keith Pratt, Jeffrey Moser, Katie Hill.1 6880-01iCover title also in Chinese:aZhongguo yi shu 1aLondon :bPhaidon Press Limited ;aNew York, NY :bPhaidon Press Inc.,c2013.  a350 pages :billustrations (chiefly color) ;c30 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  astill imagebsti2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes bibliographical references and index.  a"The Chinese Art Book examines the art of the oldest continuous civilization on earth. Full of surprises for the reader new to Chinese art as well as for specialists, its unique arrangement breaks new ground by pairing works that speak to one another in unexpected historical, stylistic and cultural ways. Visually exciting pages allow each object to stand alone and at the same time to be viewed in conjunction with a carefully selected companion, producing illuminating and often inspiring pairings. The dialogue between each couple invites meanings that often go far beyond those of the individual works. Every form of Chinese visual art is featured - painting, calligraphy, sculpture, ceramics, figurines, jades, bronzes, gold and silver, photography, video, installation and performance art. The works date from Neolithic cultures of the fourth millennium BC to the most recent contemporary art being produced in China, Taiwan, Hong Kong and the West"--Jacket.0 a300 works of art -- Timeline -- Artists -- Glossary and further reading -- Museums, galleries, and collections. 0aArt, Chinese. 0aArtzChinaxHistory. 0aDecorative artszChina. 7aChina.1 aMackenzie, Colinq(Colin Christopher),ewriter of introduction.1 aPratt, Keith L.,ewriter of added text.1 aMoser, Jeffrey,ewriter of added text.1 aHill, Katiec(Art lecturer),ewriter of added text.1 6246-01/$1iCover title also in Chinese:a$1!04!7o!V1KWF(B  a92bTNT  aN7340 .M23 2013wLCc1i50706010535079d9/3/2015e8/20/2015f6/10/2025g4lSTACKSmERCn1p$59.95rYsYtBOOKu8/12/2015xBOOK02836cam  2200445   u492909SIRSI20170303084818.4131115s2014    nyu           000 1 eng    a  2013043633  aDLCbengerdacDLCdYDXdYDXCPdBDXdBTCTAdOCLCOdRIOSLdNVCdILCdYUSdQGKdOCLCOdJ9UdTLEdVP@dNLGGCdOCLCQdOCLCOdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCAdCOOdGL3  c(3  a9780143123262q(pbk.)  a0143123262q(pbk.)  a(OCoLC)85223830300aPJ7916.A42bA2 2014  aMAIN1 aBalÂasim, ÚHasan.10aShort stories.kSelections.lEnglish14aThe corpse exhibition and other stories of Iraq /cHassan Blasim ; translated from the Arabic by Jonathan Wright. 1aNew York :bPenguin Books,c2014.  a196 pages ;c20 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aTranslated from Arabic.0 aThe corpse exhibition -- The killers and the compass -- The green zone rabbit -- An army newspaper -- Crosswords -- The hole -- The madman of Freedom Square -- The Iraqi Christ -- A thousand and one knives -- The composer -- The song of the goats -- The reality and the record -- That inauspicious smile -- The nightmares of Carlos Fuentes.  a"An explosive new voice in fiction emerges from Iraq in this blistering debut by "perhaps the best writer of Arabic fiction alive" (The Guardian) The first major literary work about the Iraq War from an Iraqi perspective, The Corpse Exhibition shows us the war as we have never seen it before. Here is a world not only of soldiers and assassins, hostages and car bombers, refugees and terrorists, but also of madmen and prophets, angels and djinni, sorcerers and spirits. Blending shocking realism with flights of fantasy, Hassan Blasim offers us a pageant of horrors, as haunting as the photos of Abu Ghraib and as difficult to look away from, but shot through with a gallows humor that yields an unflinching comedy of the macabre. Gripping and hallucinatory, this is a new kind of storytelling forged in the crucible of war"--cProvided by publisher.  aIngrambShelf ready books10aBalÂasim, ÚHasanvTranslations into English. 0aIraq War, 2003-2011vFiction. 7aFICTIONxShort Stories (single author) 7aFICTIONxLiterary. 7aIraq. 7aTranslations. 7aShort stories.1 aWright, Jonathan,d1953-etranslator.106240-00/(3/ra(3eLehYI bUU.(Bk(3eNJGQGJ.(Bl(3GdGfcdjRjI(B  a92bTNT  aPJ7916 .A42 A2 2014wLCc1i50706010833763d2/2/2026e12/8/2025f5/20/2025g4lSTACKSmERCn1p$15.00rYsYtBOOKu3/6/2017xBOOK01583cam  2200397   u493150SIRSI20170320101228.1020129s2001    enka          001 0 eng    a  2002265528  aUKMbengcDLCdUKMdIXAdGZMdC#PdBAKERdNLGGCdBTCTAdYDXCPdOCLCGdJPGdSINLBdGEBAYdUKBCIdBDXdKAQdEUMdOCLCFdOCLCQdOCLCOdCNGULdXFFdNGAdNZPWAdNZAUCdOCLCQ  c$1  aGBA1W39902bnb  a0714844497q(pbk.)  a9780714844497q(pbk.)  a(OCoLC)4767779700aTR820b.C35517 2001  aMAIN1 aCapa, Robert,d1913-1954.10aRobert Capa :bthe definitive collection /cRichard Whelan.  aLondon :bPhaidon,c2001.  a571 pages :billustrations, portraits ;c25 cm  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier  aIncludes index.  aPresents 937 works spanning the career--1932 to 1954--of Robert Capa, the Hungarian-born photographer best known for his images of war.  aIngrambShelf ready books10aCapa, Robert,d1913-1954xCriticism and interpretation. 0aPhotojournalism. 0aWar photography. 7aCriticism, interpretation, etc.1 aWhelan, Richard,d1946-  6500-00/$1a$1!3*!0q'`P!5E(B:The Definitive Collection.  a92bTNT  aTR820 .C35517 2001wLCc1i50706010837475f6/11/2025g4lSTACKSmERCp$45.00rYsYtBOOKu3/21/2017xBOOK03127cam  2200481   u493174SIRSI20170320101705.7050422s2005    mdu      b    001 0 eng    a  2005011159  aDLCbengcDLCdYDXdBAKERdIG#dNLGGCdOCLCQdBTCTAdYDXCPdLVBdBNMdHEBISdOCLCQdA7UdUKMGBdBDXdUPXdP4IdOCLCFdOCLCOdOCLCQdOCLCOdOCLdDEBBGdOCLCAdOCLCQdOCLCO  c(S  a0742534243q(pbk. ;qalk. paper)  a9780742534247q(pbk. ;qalk. paper)  a(OCoLC)5987950300aJC71.A7bA77 2005  aMAIN00aAristotle's Politics :bcritical essays /cedited by Richard Kraut and Steven Skultety.  aLanham :bRowman & Littlefield Publishers,c√2005.  axviii, 256 pages ;c23 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aCritical essays on the classics  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 245-254) and index.0 aAristippus in and out of Athens / Stephen Taylor Holmes -- Aristotle's social science / Stephen G. Salkever -- Political Animals and Civic Friendship / John M. Cooper -- Ideology and philosophy in Aristotle's theory of slavery / Malcolm Schofield -- Property rights in Aristotle / Fred D. Miller, Jr. -- The wisdom of the multitude : some reflections on book 3, chapter 11 of Aristotle's Politics / Jeremy Waldron -- Citizenship in Aristotle's Politics / Dorothea Frede -- Aristotle and political liberty / Jonathan Barnes -- Aristotle and anarchism / David Keyt -- Aristotle's natural democracy / Josiah Ober.1 a"Aristotle's Politics is widely recognized as one of the classics of the history of political philosophy, and like every other such masterpiece, it is a work about which there is deep division. Many readers of Aristotle are uncertain whether his Politics has any contribution to make to contemporary debates about political life and political theory. The essays in this volume sharpen this issue by addressing, implicitly or explicitly, this very question about the relevance of Aristotle's thinking in contemporary political philosophy. Written by leading scholars in lucid and accessible style, the ten essays in this volume will prove to be a critical resource for newcomers to Aristotle."--Jacket.  aIngrambShelf ready books006880-01aAristotle.tPolitics.06aAristote.tPolitique.07aPolitics (Aristotle)07aAristoteles,dv384-v322.tPolitica. 0aPolitical sciencevEarly works to 1800.17aPolitica (Aristoteles) 7aPolitical science. 7aEssays. 7aEarly works.1 aKraut, Richard,d1944-1 aSkultety, Steven. 0aCritical essays on the classics.146600-01/(Sa(SAulvxrx"fnjw(B,d384-322 (Ss(B.(S[(B.t(SSrnlxlm"a(B.  a92bTNT  aJC71 .A7 A77 2005wLCc1i50706010836865f6/4/2025g4lSTACKSmERCp$20.00rYsYtBOOKu3/21/2017xBOOK01629cam  2200409   u508261SIRSI20170918055402.3870922s1964    nyu      b    001 0 eng    a   64015222  aDLCbengcDLCdORZdLDLdYDXCPdBAKERdUKMGBdGZMdOCLCQdOCLCFdOCLCOdRCTdOCLCOdOCLdOCLCQ  c(2  a0805200754  a9780805200751  a(OCoLC)1673146000aBM550b.J813 1964  aMAIN0 aJudah,cha-Levi,dactive 12th century.14aThe Kuzari =bKitab al Khazari : an argument for the faith of Israel /cJudah Halevi ; introduction by Henry Slonimsky ; [translated from the Arabic by Hartwig Hirschfeld].  a1st Schocken paperback ed.  aNew York :bSchocken Books,c√1964.  a321 pages ;c21 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  aunmediatedbn2rdamedia  avolumebnc2rdacarrier1 aSchocken paperbacks  aIncludes bibliographical references (pages 311-313).  aIncludes indexes.  aTrans.  aIngrambShelf ready books 0aJudaismvApologetic works. 7aApologetic writings.08iOnline version:aJudah, ha-Levi, 12th cent.sKitÂab al-Úhujjah. English.tKuzari.b1st Schocken paperback ed.dNew York : Schocken Books, √1964w(OCoLC)609306092 0aSchocken paperbacks.106240-01/(2/ra(2kz`a `lgbd(B  a92bTNT  aBM550 .J813 1964wLCc1i50706010847680f5/21/2025g4lSTACKSmERCp$20.00rYsYtBOOKu9/19/2017xBOOK01641cam  2200397   u512120SIRSI20171211064848.